      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agent-runner-memory): use truncateUtf16Safe for memory flush error truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMemory flush error helpers in agent-runner-memory truncate error messages with raw UTF-16 code-unit slices. An emoji or supplementary character crossing the 200- or 600-char boundary could leave an unpaired surrogate in user-visible error messages.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace two raw `.slice(0, N)` calls in `buildMemoryFlushErrorPayload` and `truncateMemoryFlushErrorMessage` with `truncateUtf16Safe`. The existing limits, prefixes, and ellipsis behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMemory compaction flush error messages shown to users remain valid Unicode when long provider errors contain emoji or other supplementary characters at the truncation boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `npx vitest run src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-memory.test.ts` — 1 file, 47 tests passed.\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-memory.ts` | Replace raw `.slice(0,N)` with `truncateUtf16Safe` in two error formatting helpers. |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
